%I A400915 #6 Oct 14 2026 23:12:10
%S A400915 1,1,4,22,189,3249,256253
%N A400915 Number of nonisomorphic commutative g-dimonoids of order n.
%C A400915 A g-dimonoid is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A400915    (x -| y) -| z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A400915    (x -| y) |- z = x |- (y |- z).
%C A400915 A g-dimonoid (D,-|,|-) is called commutative if both (D,-|) and (D,|-) are commutative semigroups.
%H A400915 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.30970/ms.66.1.24-37">On the number of g-dimonoids of small order</a>, Mat. Stud. 66(1) (2026), 24-37.
%H A400915 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.29641">On the number of g-dimonoids of small order</a>, arXiv:2607.29641 [math.GR] (2026).
%H A400915 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22646289">Lists of all pairwise nonisomorphic commutative g-dimonoids of orders up to 6</a>, Zenodo (2026).
%H A400915 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/32700f9f64e7e7d81a79f676716b3e64">Python code for computing nonisomorphic g-dimonoids</a>, GitHub Gist (2026).
%e A400915 For n = 2, there are exactly 4 pairwise nonisomorphic commutative g-dimonoids (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all four g-dimonoids are listed below.
%e A400915 g-dimonoid #1:
%e A400915    -|:   |-:
%e A400915    0 0   0 0
%e A400915    0 0   0 0
%e A400915 g-dimonoid #2:
%e A400915    -|:   |-:
%e A400915    0 1   0 1
%e A400915    1 0   1 0
%e A400915 g-dimonoid #3:
%e A400915    -|:   |-:
%e A400915    0 0   0 0
%e A400915    0 1   0 1
%e A400915 g-dimonoid #4:
%e A400915    -|:   |-:
%e A400915    0 0   1 1
%e A400915    0 0   1 1
%Y A400915 Cf. A027851, A001426, A400914, A400568, A400569, A400570.
%K A400915 nonn,more
